From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 15:08:09 -0400
Subject: fix: finish the audit's Phase 0 and prove it on a real build

A recheck of patches 0053-0056 against PLAN.md, with the P0 items they
left open or broke finished, each proven by a test that runs in a real
browser window (stedding_browser_tests, new) or in the unit suites.

The sidebar. One rename-field watcher ends every in-place rename (tab,
folder, Space) on a click elsewhere or a blur, keeps it across a window
deactivation, and trims or drops an unchanged name (TAB-1, TAB-4,
SPC-29). A link dropped over a folder opens where the indicator shows,
at any depth, and chrome://tab-strip-internals shows folders (TAB-5).
Folder interiors are addressable: a link from a folder tab joins it, a
split nests whole and in place, Move Tabs Out keeps nested rows in the
parent, an emptied chain leaves the tree (TAB-6). Folder drops and chip
drops move tabs without detaching them, and a chip refuses a tab
group's header as it refuses an essential (TAB-9, SPC-4). Range selection
skips rows a collapsed folder hides (TAB-10). Folder title and collapse
reach observers at once (TAB-11). Folders come back after three
restarts, and after Cmd-Shift-T and a window reopened from History
(TAB-12). The rail's form follows the drawn width and hover-expand
keeps one click handler (WIN-3).

Spaces and cookie jars. Deleting the active Space shows its neighbour
first, wipes an independent jar once after its tabs left, and asks
first (SPC-20, SPC-24). The settings page observes the registry and
every SpaceModel observer is told the model is going (SPC-1, WEB-2). A
tab's Space, and so its jar, is chosen before its contents exist; a
page opened without an opener is made again in its Space's jar; a typed
address in a fresh tab moves the tab to the routed jar first; routes
apply only to tabs Stedding made, and searches skip "contains" rules
(SPC-12, CMD-8). A page with unsaved changes keeps its jar until it is
left, and a form it sends goes in the session it was filled in; the new
tab page and settings live in the profile's jar and the
first web page a tab leaves them for is made in its Space's jar; a
change of isolation asks first, with the number of pages it reloads
(SPC-9). Contents replaced by a sleep or a jar rebind keep the name and
the jar, and the session file a restart reads holds the tab's Space,
pin, home and name again (TAB-15, SPC-8); isolation applies in every
window (SPC-13), pin homes are web pages only (TAB-17).

Closing the last tab of the active Space no longer makes another
Space's tab active until a posted task opens a new one: the strip asks
the Space before a close, and the Space adds its new tab first, so the
close activates it. That turn used to flash the other Space's page, and
a sleeping tab there woke and reloaded (spaces B4; a page whose
beforeunload may keep it, and a tab dragged into another window, still
get the fix after the close).

The switcher and Clear. A chip dragged along the row or down the rail
follows the pointer and the chips it passes step aside to show where it
lands; a drag that loses the pointer puts them back; a right-to-left row
is measured mirrored, and Move Left moves a chip left on screen
(SPC-6). A Space comes back to a tab that arrived active -- Cmd-T, a
link opened in a new tab -- because the tab is filed before the
activation is recorded (spaces B2). The Clear line takes presses from
its bounds, not from its last paint, and Cmd-Shift-K works in a private
window (CMD-3, SPC-7). A second screenshot asked for while one runs
waits its turn and gets its own file (WIN-2). A folder collapsed from
any path -- its header, the command bar, a session rebuild -- hides its
rows at once: the rows used to follow only once a pass had reached that
folder's view, so a folder made and collapsed at once kept them (SPC-5).
The tab menu's Close row takes the plural with a selection, as its other
rows do ("Close 2 Tabs"; TAB-10, tabs R21). The command bar no longer
offers a switch that turns Peek on while Peek is withdrawn (CMD-4,
decision 2).

The rest. Little windows open in upstream's safe profile, refuse a
profile that may not open a window, and give an untrusted launch an
opaque initiator (CMD-7). The keychain read fails closed and copies a
legacy key once, for an existing profile only; the profile migration
runs before Crashpad (WEB-1, PLT-1, PLT-2). DuckDuckGo is the fallback
search in every region, the choice program runs everywhere through one
check, and the regional cases assert that (WEB-4). The archive sweep
leaves tabs in use alone and an archived tab comes back to its Space,
folder and jar (WEB-6, WEB-7). A bare Escape closes a little window on
the Mac. Private is decided once, from the profile, and the window says
so on its colour key: a normal dark window with Chrome's Grey is no
longer painted graphite, and a Guest window is not labelled Private
(WIN-4). A build started with --stedding-stay-in-background never makes
itself the front app, so tooling/capture-state can photograph a state
while someone works at the machine. Settings -> Stedding's "Expand the
collapsed sidebar" switch is bound to vertical_tabs.expand_on_hover
again: M155 renamed the pref, and the switch had done nothing since the
move (settings T6).

Why: the September 2026 audit (PLAN.md) found these features broken or
unproven; patches 0053-0056 claimed the plan done without a build.
Removable when: the Phase 4 re-cut (PLAN.md SER-4) folds these fixes
into the feature patches they belong to.
