+// Tabs dragged onto a folder's header and onto a Space's chip (PLAN.md
+// TAB-9, SPC-4, TST-7). A real window's rows are pressed, dragged in steps
+// and released through the window's root view. The tabs move without leaving
+// the window: the same tab and page, with its pin, home, Space and place in
+// the Space's recent list. The drops used to detach the tabs and insert them
+// again -- routing them to another Space on the way, and tearing a window
+// off when the pointer left the list for the switcher.
